#+TITLE: E6's GNU Emacs Config
#+AUTHOR: Elihu SoNy (Ehesh)
#+STARTUP: overview
#+OPTIONS: toc:3

After years of trying to use Emacs and failing — partly because I could never get the hang of it, partly because it frustrated me on Windows — I'm finally finding my way here. This is a writing-first scholarly environment: a reliable scholar's desk inside a mindscape library and planning war room.

The base comes from Derek Taylor's config, absorbed into the Xero Linux configurations, then rebuilt on top of Minimal Emacs.d. From there I've drawn on Kristoffer Balintona's articles and chi-xigua's PovertEmacs. Modal editing is handled by Meow. The external ecosystem (Zotero, Yazi, Quarto, Graphify) stays outside Emacs.

Sources:
- Minimal Emacs: https://github.com/jamescherti/minimal-emacs.d
- Kristoffer Balintona: https://kristofferbalintona.me/
- PovertEmacs: https://codeberg.org/chi-xigua/PovertEmacs

