* Auto-Tangle Configuration

Automatically tangle this config file on save so the generated =.el= files stay in sync.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp :tangle no
(defun org-babel-tangle-on-save ()
  "Tangle the current Org file on save."
  (when (string= (file-name-extension (buffer-file-name)) "org")
    (org-babel-tangle)))

(add-hook 'org-mode-hook
          (lambda ()
            (add-hook 'before-save-hook #'org-babel-tangle-on-save nil 'local)))
#+end_src

* Startup & Performance
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/pre-early-init.el
:END:

These settings land in =pre-early-init.el=, which minimal-emacs.d loads /before/ its own =early-init.el=. Only things that must be set before Emacs's early-init phase runs belong here: disabling the built-in package manager, directory layout, and anti-flicker UI suppression. No packages, no =use-package=.

** File Header

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
;;; pre-early-init.el --- Pre-early init -*- no-byte-compile: t; lexical-binding: t; -*-
#+end_src

** Disable package.el

Elpaca replaces the built-in package manager. Disable it before anything else touches it.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(setq package-enable-at-startup nil)
#+end_src

** Scripts

Add the scripts directory to the load path and bootstrap Elpaca. The =elpaca-setup.el= script lives at =~/.emacs.d/var/scripts/elpaca-setup.el=.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "~/.emacs.d/var/scripts/")
(require 'elpaca-setup)
#+end_src

** Directory Layout & QoS

Redirect all of Emacs's runtime files (caches, backups, auto-saves) into =var/= to keep the root =~/.emacs.d/= clean. The default working directory is set here so new frames open in the right place.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
;; Redirect var files into ~/.emacs.d/var/
(setq minimal-emacs-var-dir (expand-file-name "var/" minimal-emacs-user-directory))
(setq user-emacs-directory minimal-emacs-var-dir)

;; Default working directory for new frames
(setq default-directory "~/projects/Story-Weaver")
#+end_src

** Anti-flicker UI

Suppress bars before the first frame is drawn — setting these later causes a visible layout jump. Must live in =pre-early-init.el=.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(menu-bar-mode -1)
(scroll-bar-mode -1)
(tool-bar-mode -1)
(setq use-file-dialog nil)
(setq use-dialog-box nil)
(setq pop-up-windows nil)
#+end_src

** Backup

Send all backup files to a dedicated directory so they never litter the project tree.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(setq backup-directory-alist '(("." . "~/.emacs.d/var/backups/")))
#+end_src

* Typography & Fonts
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/pre-init.el
:END:

Fonts land in =pre-init.el= (loaded just before =init.el=). Elpaca is already bootstrapped from the script loaded in =pre-early-init.el=, so =use-package= works here.

** File Header

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
;;; pre-init.el --- Pre-init -*- no-byte-compile: t; lexical-binding: t; -*-
#+end_src

** Nerd Icons

Provides icon glyphs used throughout: Dashboard, Dired, completion UIs, and the modeline. Loaded early so downstream packages can depend on it.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package nerd-icons
  :ensure t)
#+end_src

** Fontaine

[[https://github.com/protesilaos/fontaine][Fontaine]] manages named font presets. ~regular~ is the everyday writing preset; ~large~ inherits it with bigger sizes for presentation or accessibility.

- Fixed pitch: FiraCode Nerd Font (code blocks, tables)
- Variable pitch: Gentium Plus (prose, headings)

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package fontaine
  :ensure t
  :custom
  (fontaine-presets
   '((regular
      :default-family "FiraCode Nerd Font"
      :default-weight medium
      :default-height 110
      :fixed-pitch-family "FiraCode Nerd Font"
      :fixed-pitch-weight nil
      :fixed-pitch-height 1.0
      :variable-pitch-family "Gentium Plus"
      :variable-pitch-weight normal
      :variable-pitch-height 1.2
      :line-spacing 1)
     (large
      :inherit regular
      :default-height 175
      :variable-pitch-height 1.3)))
  :config
  (fontaine-set-preset 'regular))
#+end_src

* Theme & Appearance
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

Everything from here onward tangles to =post-init.el=, which runs after =init.el= with Elpaca fully available.

** File Header (post-init.el)

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
;;; post-init.el --- Post-init -*- no-byte-compile: t; lexical-binding: t; -*-
#+end_src

** Custom Safe Themes

Themes approved to load without a confirmation prompt.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(setq custom-safe-themes
      '("02f57ef0a20b7f61adce51445b68b2a7e832648ce2e7efb19d217b6454c1b644"
        "6945dadc749ac5cbd47012cad836f92aea9ebec9f504d32fe89a956260773ca4"
        "944d52450c57b7cbba08f9b3d08095eb7a5541b0ecfb3a0a9ecd4a18f3c28948"
        "636b135e4b7c86ac41375da39ade929e2bd6439de8901f53f88fde7dd5ac3561"
        "1f669e8abe4dc2855268c9a607b5e350e2811b3c5afd09af5939ff0c01a89c5a"))
#+end_src

** ef-themes

[[https://github.com/protesilaos/ef-themes][ef-themes]] by Protesilaos Stavrou. ~ef-owl~ (dark) and ~ef-frost~ (light) are toggled with =<f5>=. The ~ef-frost~ palette override softens the hover highlight.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package ef-themes
  :ensure t
  :config
  (setq ef-frost-palette-overrides
        '((bg-hover "#b3efdf")))
  (setq ef-themes-to-toggle '(ef-owl ef-frost))
  (load-theme 'ef-owl t))

(keymap-global-set "<f5>" #'ef-themes-toggle)
#+end_src

** Diminish

Hides minor-mode lighters from the modeline when =:diminish= is specified in a =use-package= block.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package diminish
  :ensure t)
(elpaca-wait)
#+end_src

* Core Editing
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

Baseline editing behaviour. All of these belong in =post-init.el= — they depend on Emacs being fully initialised and several require the frame to exist.

** Sane Defaults

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(delete-selection-mode 1)    ; Typing replaces the active region
(electric-indent-mode -1)    ; No surprise auto-indentation
(electric-pair-mode 1)       ; Auto-close parens, brackets, quotes

;; Prevent <> from auto-pairing in Org (would break <s TAB tempo expansion)
(add-hook 'org-mode-hook
          (lambda ()
            (setq-local electric-pair-inhibit-predicate
                        `(lambda (c)
                           (if (char-equal c ?<) t
                             (,electric-pair-inhibit-predicate c))))))

(global-auto-revert-mode t)          ; Reload files changed on disk
(global-display-line-numbers-mode 1) ; Line numbers everywhere
(global-visual-line-mode t)          ; Wrap long lines visually

;; Org src block indentation
(setq org-edit-src-content-indentation 0) ; No extra indent in src blocks
(setq org-src-preserve-indentation t)     ; Preserve indentation on tangle
#+end_src

** Minibuffer Escape

Single =ESC= quits the minibuffer instead of requiring three presses.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(keymap-global-set "<escape>" #'keyboard-escape-quit)
#+end_src

** Prettify Symbols

Replaces certain ASCII sequences with prettier Unicode glyphs in supported modes (e.g. =->= → →).

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(global-prettify-symbols-mode t)
#+end_src

** Zoom Keybindings

=C-==/=C--= and the mouse wheel scale text in the current buffer.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(keymap-global-set "C-=" #'text-scale-increase)
(keymap-global-set "C--" #'text-scale-decrease)
;; Mouse wheel events are finicky with the new keymap-global-set syntax;
;; use global-set-key + kbd here to avoid key-valid-p rejecting <C-wheel-*>.
(global-set-key (kbd "<C-wheel-up>")   #'text-scale-increase)
(global-set-key (kbd "<C-wheel-down>") #'text-scale-decrease)
#+end_src

** Drag Stuff

[[https://github.com/rejeep/drag-stuff.el][drag-stuff]] lets you drag words, regions, or lines with =M-up/down/left/right=.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package drag-stuff
  :ensure t
  :diminish
  :init
  (drag-stuff-global-mode 1)
  (drag-stuff-define-keys))
#+end_src

** Ediff

Use a horizontal split and keep the control panel in the same frame. =j/k= moves between diffs.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(setq ediff-split-window-function 'split-window-horizontally
      ediff-window-setup-function 'ediff-setup-windows-plain)

(defun e6/ediff-hook ()
  (ediff-setup-keymap)
  (define-key ediff-mode-map "j" 'ediff-next-difference)
  (define-key ediff-mode-map "k" 'ediff-previous-difference))

(add-hook 'ediff-mode-hook #'e6/ediff-hook)
#+end_src

* Modal Editing — Meow
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

[[https://github.com/meow-edit/meow][Meow]] is a modal editing mode that integrates cleanly with Emacs's own keybindings rather than overlaying a Vim emulation layer. The leader key (=SPC= in normal state) is wired to the Transient menus defined in the next section — so the leader key bindings are set /after/ the menus exist.

** Meow Setup

Standard qwerty layout. Motion state (used in special buffers like Dired, Help, etc.) overrides =j/k= for line movement. Normal state follows Meow's own design — no Vim cargo-culting.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package meow
  :ensure t
  :config
  (defun meow-setup ()
    (setq meow-cheatsheet-layout meow-cheatsheet-layout-qwerty)

    ;; Motion state — special/read-only buffers
    (meow-motion-overwrite-define-key
     '("j" . meow-next)
     '("k" . meow-prev)
     '("<escape>" . ignore))

    ;; Normal state — full editing key map
    (meow-normal-define-key
     '("0" . meow-expand-0)
     '("9" . meow-expand-9)
     '("8" . meow-expand-8)
     '("7" . meow-expand-7)
     '("6" . meow-expand-6)
     '("5" . meow-expand-5)
     '("4" . meow-expand-4)
     '("3" . meow-expand-3)
     '("2" . meow-expand-2)
     '("1" . meow-expand-1)
     '("-" . negative-argument)
     '(";" . meow-reverse)
     '("," . meow-inner-of-thing)
     '("." . meow-bounds-of-thing)
     '("[" . meow-beginning-of-thing)
     '("]" . meow-end-of-thing)
     '("a" . meow-append)
     '("A" . meow-open-below)
     '("b" . meow-back-word)
     '("B" . meow-back-symbol)
     '("c" . meow-change)
     '("d" . meow-delete)
     '("D" . meow-backward-delete)
     '("e" . meow-next-word)
     '("E" . meow-next-symbol)
     '("f" . meow-find)
     '("g" . meow-cancel)
     '("G" . meow-grab)
     '("h" . meow-left)
     '("H" . meow-left-expand)
     '("i" . meow-insert)
     '("I" . meow-open-above)
     '("j" . meow-next)
     '("J" . meow-next-expand)
     '("k" . meow-prev)
     '("K" . meow-prev-expand)
     '("l" . meow-right)
     '("L" . meow-right-expand)
     '("m" . meow-join)
     '("n" . meow-search)
     '("o" . meow-block)
     '("O" . meow-to-block)
     '("p" . meow-yank)
     '("q" . meow-quit)
     '("r" . meow-replace)
     '("R" . meow-swap)
     '("s" . meow-kill)
     '("t" . meow-till)
     '("u" . meow-undo)
     '("U" . meow-undo-in-selection)
     '("v" . meow-visit)
     '("w" . meow-next-word)
     '("W" . meow-next-symbol)
     '("x" . meow-line)
     '("y" . meow-save)
     '("z" . meow-pop-selection)
     '("'" . repeat)
     '("<escape>" . ignore)))

  (meow-setup)
  (meow-global-mode 1))

;; Wait for Meow to be ready before the Transient menus wire to the leader
(elpaca-wait)
#+end_src

* Completion Stack
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

The stack is: Vertico (vertical minibuffer UI) → Orderless (fuzzy matching) → Marginalia (annotations) → Embark (contextual actions) → Consult (enhanced commands) → Corfu (in-buffer popup) → Cape (completion-at-point extensions).

Do not replace these tools casually — explain interaction effects before changing anything here.

** Vertico

Vertical completion interface for the minibuffer.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package vertico
  :ensure t
  :bind (:map vertico-map
         ("C-j" . vertico-next)
         ("C-k" . vertico-previous)
         ("C-f" . vertico-exit)
         :map minibuffer-local-map
         ("M-h" . backward-kill-word))
  :custom
  (vertico-cycle t)
  :init
  (vertico-mode)
  (vertico-mouse-mode))
#+end_src

** Orderless

Flexible, space-separated completion matching. The =file= category falls back to =partial-completion= for path segments.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package orderless
  :ensure t
  :custom
  (completion-styles '(basic partial-completion orderless))
  (completion-category-defaults nil)
  (completion-category-overrides '((file (styles partial-completion)))))
#+end_src

** Marginalia

Adds rich annotations (docstrings, file sizes, key descriptions) next to minibuffer candidates.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package marginalia
  :ensure t
  :after vertico
  :custom
  (marginalia-annotators '(marginalia-annotators-heavy marginalia-annotators-light nil))
  :init
  (marginalia-mode))

(use-package nerd-icons-completion
  :ensure t
  :after (marginalia nerd-icons)
  :hook (marginalia-mode . nerd-icons-completion-marginalia-setup)
  :init
  (nerd-icons-completion-mode))
#+end_src

** Embark

Context-sensitive actions on minibuffer candidates and things at point. =C-.= acts; =C-;= does the most sensible thing (dwim).

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package embark
  :ensure t
  :bind
  (("C-."   . embark-act)
   ("C-;"   . embark-dwim)
   ("C-h B" . embark-bindings))
  :init
  (setq prefix-help-command #'embark-prefix-help-command)
  :config
  (add-to-list 'display-buffer-alist
               '("\\`\\*Embark Collect \\(Live\\|Completions\\)\\*"
                 nil
                 (window-parameters (mode-line-format . none)))))

(use-package embark-consult
  :ensure t
  :hook (embark-collect-mode . consult-preview-at-point-mode))
#+end_src

** Consult

Enhanced versions of standard Emacs commands with live preview and narrowing. Replaces all Counsel/Ivy commands.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package consult
  :ensure t
  :after vertico
  :hook (completion-list-mode . consult-preview-at-point-mode)
  :bind (("C-x b"   . consult-buffer)
         ("C-x 4 b" . consult-buffer-other-window)
         ("C-x 5 b" . consult-buffer-other-frame)
         ("C-x r b" . consult-bookmark)
         ("M-y"     . consult-yank-pop)
         ("M-g e"   . consult-compile-error)
         ("M-g f"   . consult-flymake)
         ("M-g g"   . consult-goto-line)
         ("M-g M-g" . consult-goto-line)
         ("M-g o"   . consult-outline)
         ("M-g i"   . consult-imenu)
         ("M-g I"   . consult-imenu-multi)
         ("M-s d"   . consult-find)
         ("M-s g"   . consult-grep)
         ("M-s G"   . consult-git-grep)
         ("M-s r"   . consult-ripgrep)
         ("M-s l"   . consult-line)
         ("M-s L"   . consult-line-multi)
         :map isearch-mode-map
         ("M-s l"   . consult-line)
         :map minibuffer-local-map
         ("M-s"     . consult-history)
         ("M-r"     . consult-history))
  :init
  (setq register-preview-delay 0.5
        register-preview-function #'consult-register-format)
  (advice-add #'register-preview :override #'consult-register-window)
  (setq xref-show-xrefs-function #'consult-xref
        xref-show-definitions-function #'consult-xref)
  :config
  (consult-customize
   consult-theme :preview-key '(:debounce 0.2 any)
   consult-ripgrep consult-git-grep consult-grep
   consult-bookmark consult-recent-file consult-xref
   consult--source-bookmark consult--source-file-register
   consult--source-recent-file consult--source-project-recent-file
   :preview-key '(:debounce 0.4 any))
  (setq consult-narrow-key "<"))
#+end_src

** Corfu

In-buffer completion popup. Triggered manually with =TAB= (=tab-always-indent 'complete=) — auto-popup is off to avoid interrupting prose writing.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package corfu
  :ensure t
  :hook ((prog-mode   . corfu-mode)
         (shell-mode  . corfu-mode)
         (eshell-mode . corfu-mode))
  :bind (:map corfu-map
         ("C-n"      . corfu-next)
         ("C-p"      . corfu-previous)
         ("<escape>"  . corfu-quit)
         ("<return>"  . corfu-insert)
         ("C-g"      . corfu-quit)
         ("M-d"      . corfu-show-documentation)
         ("M-l"      . corfu-show-location))
  :custom
  (read-extended-command-predicate #'command-completion-default-include-p)
  (text-mode-ispell-word-completion nil)
  (tab-always-indent 'complete)
  (completion-cycle-threshold nil)
  (corfu-auto nil)             ; Manual trigger only — keeps prose writing clean
  (corfu-auto-prefix 2)
  (corfu-auto-delay 0.25)
  (corfu-min-width 80)
  (corfu-max-width corfu-min-width)
  (corfu-count 14)
  (corfu-scroll-margin 4)
  (corfu-cycle nil)
  (corfu-quit-at-boundary nil)
  (corfu-separator ?\s)
  (corfu-quit-no-match 'separator)
  (corfu-preview-current 'insert)
  (corfu-preselect-first t)
  (corfu-echo-documentation nil)
  (lsp-completion-provider :none)
  :init
  (global-corfu-mode)
  :config
  (defun corfu-enable-in-minibuffer ()
    "Enable Corfu in the minibuffer when Vertico is not active."
    (unless (or (bound-and-true-p mct--active)
                (bound-and-true-p vertico--input))
      (setq-local corfu-auto nil)
      (corfu-mode 1)))
  (add-hook 'minibuffer-setup-hook #'corfu-enable-in-minibuffer 1))

(use-package kind-icon
  :ensure t
  :after corfu
  :custom
  (kind-icon-use-icons t)
  (kind-icon-default-face 'corfu-default)
  (kind-icon-blend-background nil)
  (kind-icon-blend-frac 0.08)
  :config
  (add-to-list 'corfu-margin-formatters #'kind-icon-margin-formatter)
  ;; Reset icon cache when the theme changes so colours stay in sync
  (add-hook 'ef-themes-post-load-hook #'kind-icon-reset-cache))
#+end_src

** Cape

Completion-at-point extensions: dynamic abbreviation, file path, and Elisp block completion in Org src blocks.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package cape
  :ensure t
  :bind ("C-c p" . cape-prefix-map)
  :init
  (add-hook 'completion-at-point-functions #'cape-dabbrev)
  (add-hook 'completion-at-point-functions #'cape-file)
  (add-hook 'completion-at-point-functions #'cape-elisp-block))
#+end_src

* Keybindings — Transient Menus
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

All keybindings live here. The approach: Transient menus group related commands, wired to =SPC + letter= via Meow's leader. No general.el, no Evil states.

Transient must load before the menus are defined. The Meow leader bindings (last block in this section) wire everything together — they must come /after/ all =transient-define-prefix= calls.

** Transient Setup

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package transient
  :ensure t
  :config
  (setq transient-enable-popup-navigation t))

(elpaca-wait)
#+end_src

