** Windows Menu

Window navigation and management. =H/J/K/L= (uppercase) swap the window's buffer with its neighbour using =windmove-swap-states-in-direction= (built-in since Emacs 27).

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(transient-define-prefix e6/windows-menu ()
  "Windows"
  [["Navigate"
    ("h" "Left"              windmove-left)
    ("j" "Down"              windmove-down)
    ("k" "Up"                windmove-up)
    ("l" "Right"             windmove-right)
    ("w" "Next window"       other-window)]
   ["Split / Close"
    ("s" "Horizontal split"  split-window-below)
    ("v" "Vertical split"    split-window-right)
    ("c" "Close window"      delete-window)
    ("n" "New window"        split-window-right)]
   ["Swap buffers"
    ("H" "Swap left"
     (lambda () (interactive) (windmove-swap-states-in-direction 'left)))
    ("J" "Swap down"
     (lambda () (interactive) (windmove-swap-states-in-direction 'down)))
    ("K" "Swap up"
     (lambda () (interactive) (windmove-swap-states-in-direction 'up)))
    ("L" "Swap right"
     (lambda () (interactive) (windmove-swap-states-in-direction 'right)))]
   ["Words"
    ("d" "Downcase word"     downcase-word)
    ("u" "Upcase word"       upcase-word)
    ("=" "Count words"       count-words)]])
#+end_src

** Meow Leader Bindings

Wire =SPC + letter= to the menus above. This block must come /after/ all =transient-define-prefix= calls so Meow can resolve the symbols.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'meow
  (meow-leader-define-key
   ;; Quick-access commands
   '("SPC" . execute-extended-command)
   '("."   . find-file)
   '(","   . consult-buffer)
   '("TAB" . comment-line)
   '("u"   . universal-argument)
   ;; Menu groups
   '("b"   . e6/buffers-menu)
   '("d"   . e6/dired-menu)
   '("e"   . e6/eval-menu)
   '("f"   . e6/files-menu)
   '("g"   . e6/git-menu)
   '("h"   . e6/help-menu)
   '("m"   . e6/org-menu)
   '("o"   . e6/open-menu)
   '("p"   . projectile-command-map)
   '("r"   . e6/radio-menu)
   '("s"   . e6/search-menu)
   '("t"   . e6/toggle-menu)
   '("w"   . e6/windows-menu)
   ;; Perspective
   '("="   . perspective-map)))
#+end_src

* Writing Environment
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

** Org Mode

*** Org Tempo

=org-tempo= is a built-in Org module that enables =<s TAB= → =#+BEGIN_SRC … #+END_SRC= and similar structural shortcuts.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(require 'org-tempo)
#+end_src

*** TOC-Org

Maintains the =:toc:= heading's table of contents automatically on save.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package toc-org
  :ensure t
  :commands toc-org-enable
  :init (add-hook 'org-mode-hook #'toc-org-enable))
#+end_src

*** Org Indent Diminish

Removes the "Ind" lighter from the modeline.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'org-indent
  (diminish 'org-indent-mode))
#+end_src

*** Org Modern

[[https://github.com/minad/org-modern][org-modern]] replaces Org's ASCII decorations with clean Unicode: prettier stars, checkboxes, tables. Agenda styled to match.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package org-modern
  :ensure t
  :config
  (setq org-auto-align-tags nil
        org-tags-column 0
        org-catch-invisible-edits 'show-and-error
        org-insert-heading-respect-content t
        org-modern-star 'replace
        org-agenda-tags-column 0
        org-agenda-block-separator ?─
        org-agenda-time-grid
        '((daily today require-timed)
          (800 1000 1200 1400 1600 1800 2000)
          " ┄┄┄┄┄ " "┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄")
        org-agenda-current-time-string
        "◀── now ─────────────────────────────────────────────────")
  (setq org-ellipsis "…")
  (set-face-attribute 'org-ellipsis nil :inherit 'default :box nil)
  (global-org-modern-mode))
#+end_src

*** Org Modern Indent

Fixes indentation rendering inside org-modern source blocks.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
;; Pause and let Elpaca finish its queue before loading GitHub-recipe packages.
;; Without this, packages with :ensure (:host github ...) can race against
;; elpaca-use-package integration being fully active.
(elpaca-wait)

(use-package org-modern-indent
  :ensure (:host github :repo "jdtsmith/org-modern-indent")
  :hook (org-mode . org-modern-indent-mode))
#+end_src

*** Org Appear

Makes emphasis markers (=*bold*=, =/italic/=, etc.) visible only while the cursor is on them, keeping prose readable without sacrificing editability.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package org-appear
  :ensure t
  :hook (org-mode . org-appear-mode))
#+end_src

*** Org Menu

[[https://github.com/sheijk/org-menu][org-menu]] provides a context-sensitive Transient menu for Org actions, triggered from within Org buffers.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package org-menu
  :ensure (:host github :repo "sheijk/org-menu"))
#+end_src

** Citar

[[https://github.com/emacs-citar/citar][Citar]] integrates with Zotero via Better BibTeX. Export your library to a =.bib= file with "Keep updated" enabled; Citar sees every reference you add. Embark integration gives contextual citation actions.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package citar
  :ensure t
  :custom
  (citar-bibliography '("~/Documents/references.bib"))
  (citar-library-paths '("~/Zotero/storage/"))
  (citar-notes-paths '("~/Documents/notes/"))
  :bind
  (("C-c b" . citar-insert-citation)
   :map org-mode-map
   ("C-c b" . org-cite-insert))
  :config
  (setq org-cite-insert-processor 'citar
        org-cite-follow-processor 'citar
        org-cite-activate-processor 'citar))

(use-package citar-embark
  :ensure t
  :after (citar embark)
  :no-require
  :config (citar-embark-mode))
#+end_src

** Writeroom

Distraction-free writing mode: centred 90-character column, maximised frame, modeline preserved so you can still see state.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package writeroom-mode
  :ensure t
  :commands (writeroom-mode global-writeroom-mode)
  :custom
  (writeroom-width 90)
  (writeroom-mode-line t)
  (writeroom-fullscreen-effect 'maximized))
#+end_src

** Write Good Mode

Highlights weasel words, passive voice, and similar prose weaknesses. Activate on demand via =SPC t w= or =M-x writegood-mode=.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package writegood-mode
  :ensure t
  :commands writegood-mode)
#+end_src

* File Management
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

Yazi handles heavy file management externally. Dired covers in-Emacs needs. Neotree provides a sidebar for project orientation.

** Dired

=dired-open= maps file extensions to external viewers. =peep-dired= shows previews in a split.

The =h/l= bindings for navigating up/into directories and =j/k= for peep-browsing use =keymap-set= — no Evil dependency.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package dired-open
  :ensure t
  :config
  (setq dired-open-extensions '(("gif" . "sxiv")
                                ("jpg" . "sxiv")
                                ("png" . "sxiv")
                                ("mkv" . "mpv")
                                ("mp4" . "mpv"))))

(use-package peep-dired
  :ensure t
  :after dired
  :config
  (keymap-set dired-mode-map     "h" #'dired-up-directory)
  (keymap-set dired-mode-map     "l" #'dired-open-file)
  (keymap-set peep-dired-mode-map "j" #'peep-dired-next-file)
  (keymap-set peep-dired-mode-map "k" #'peep-dired-prev-file))
#+end_src

** Nerd Icons Dired

Shows nerd-icons glyphs next to filenames in Dired buffers.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package nerd-icons-dired
  :ensure t
  :after nerd-icons
  :hook (dired-mode . nerd-icons-dired-mode))
#+end_src

** Neotree

File-tree sidebar. =neo-smart-open= makes it jump to the current file on open.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package neotree
  :ensure t
  :config
  (setq neo-smart-open t
        neo-show-hidden-files t
        neo-window-width 55
        neo-window-fixed-size nil
        inhibit-compacting-font-caches t
        projectile-switch-project-action 'neotree-projectile-action)
  (add-hook 'neo-after-create-hook
            (lambda (_)
              (with-current-buffer (get-buffer neo-buffer-name)
                (setq truncate-lines t
                      word-wrap nil)
                (make-local-variable 'auto-hscroll-mode)
                (setq auto-hscroll-mode nil)))))
#+end_src

* UI & Cosmetics
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

** Dashboard

Startup screen showing recent files, agenda, bookmarks, and projects. Update the banner path if the image moves.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package dashboard
  :ensure t
  :demand t
  :init
  (setq initial-buffer-choice 'dashboard-open
        dashboard-set-heading-icons t
        dashboard-set-file-icons t
        dashboard-banner-logo-title "Eheshiu's cute EMACS!"
        dashboard-startup-banner "~/.emacs.d/var/images/catboy050.png"
        dashboard-center-content t
        dashboard-items '((recents   . 5)
                          (agenda    . 5)
                          (bookmarks . 3)
                          (projects  . 3)
                          (registers . 3)))
  :custom
  (dashboard-modify-heading-icons '((recents   . "file-text")
                                    (bookmarks . "book")))
  :config
  (dashboard-setup-startup-hook))
#+end_src

** Moody + Minions

[[https://github.com/tarsius/moody][Moody]] gives the modeline a clean tab/ribbon appearance. [[https://github.com/tarsius/minions][Minions]] collapses minor mode lighters into a single icon.

The modeline background colour changes when Meow enters insert state — a visual mode indicator that doesn't depend on cursor shape.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defun e6/update-modeline-for-meow-state ()
  "Set mode-line background to reflect the current Meow state."
  (let ((insert-color (ef-themes-get-color-value 'bg-hover-secondary))
        (normal-color (ef-themes-get-color-value 'bg-mode-line)))
    (if (meow-insert-mode-p)
        (set-face-attribute 'mode-line nil :background insert-color)
      (set-face-attribute 'mode-line nil :background normal-color))))

(add-hook 'meow-insert-enter-hook #'e6/update-modeline-for-meow-state)
(add-hook 'meow-insert-exit-hook  #'e6/update-modeline-for-meow-state)
(add-hook 'meow-normal-enter-hook #'e6/update-modeline-for-meow-state)

(use-package moody
  :ensure t
  :config
  (moody-replace-mode-line-front-space)
  (moody-replace-mode-line-buffer-identification)
  (moody-replace-vc-mode))

(use-package minions
  :ensure t
  :config
  (setq minions-mode-line-lighter ""
        minions-mode-line-delimiters '("" . ""))
  (minions-mode 1))
#+end_src

** Which-key

Shows available key completions after a short idle delay. Useful for discovering Transient menu entries without opening them.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package which-key
  :ensure t
  :diminish
  :init (which-key-mode 1)
  :config
  (setq which-key-side-window-location 'bottom
        which-key-sort-order #'which-key-key-order-alpha
        which-key-sort-uppercase-first nil
        which-key-add-column-padding 1
        which-key-max-display-columns nil
        which-key-min-display-lines 6
        which-key-side-window-slot -10
        which-key-side-window-max-height 0.25
        which-key-idle-delay 0.8
        which-key-max-description-length 25
        which-key-separator " → "))
#+end_src

** Highlight TODO

Highlights =TODO=, =FIXME=, =HACK=, =NOTE=, =REVIEW=, and =DEPRECATED= in source and Org buffers.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package hl-todo
  :ensure t
  :hook ((org-mode  . hl-todo-mode)
         (prog-mode . hl-todo-mode))
  :config
  (setq hl-todo-highlight-punctuation ":"
        hl-todo-keyword-faces
        `(("TODO"       warning bold)
          ("FIXME"      error bold)
          ("HACK"       font-lock-constant-face bold)
          ("REVIEW"     font-lock-keyword-face bold)
          ("NOTE"       success bold)
          ("DEPRECATED" font-lock-doc-face bold))))
#+end_src

** Rainbow Delimiters

Colour-codes nested parentheses in Elisp and Clojure. Useful when editing config blocks.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package rainbow-delimiters
  :ensure t
  :hook ((emacs-lisp-mode . rainbow-delimiters-mode)
         (clojure-mode    . rainbow-delimiters-mode)))
#+end_src

** Rainbow Mode

Renders hex colour values (=#ffffff=, =rgb(…)=) as inline background swatches.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package rainbow-mode
  :ensure t
  :diminish
  :hook (org-mode prog-mode))
#+end_src

* Utilities
:PROPERTIES:
:header-args:emacs-lisp: :tangle ~/.emacs.d/post-init.el
:END:

** PDF Tools

[[https://github.com/vedang/pdf-tools][pdf-tools]] replaces DocView for PDF viewing using poppler. Line numbers and blinking cursor are disabled in PDF view — they serve no purpose there.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package pdf-tools
  :ensure t
  :defer t
  :mode "\\.pdf\\'"
  :init (pdf-loader-install)
  :config
  (add-to-list 'revert-without-query ".pdf"))

(add-hook 'pdf-view-mode-hook
          (lambda ()
            (display-line-numbers-mode -1)
            (blink-cursor-mode -1)))
#+end_src

** Perspective

[[https://github.com/nex3/perspective-el][Perspective]] provides named workspaces, each with its own buffer list and window layout. State is persisted to disk and restored on the next session.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package perspective
  :ensure t
  :custom
  (persp-mode-prefix-key (kbd "C-c M-p"))
  :init
  (persp-mode)
  :config
  (setq persp-state-default-file "~/.emacs.d/var/sessions"))

(add-hook 'ibuffer-hook
          (lambda ()
            (persp-ibuffer-set-filter-groups)
            (unless (eq ibuffer-sorting-mode 'alphabetic)
              (ibuffer-do-sort-by-alphabetic))))

(add-hook 'kill-emacs-hook #'persp-state-save)
#+end_src

** Undo Tree

Visualises Emacs's branching undo history as a tree.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package undo-tree
  :ensure t
  :diminish undo-tree-mode
  :bind ("C-c w u" . undo-tree-visualize)
  :custom
  (undo-tree-auto-save-history nil)
  :config
  (global-undo-tree-mode))
#+end_src

** Git Time Machine

[[https://github.com/emacsmirror/git-timemachine][git-timemachine]] steps through a file's git history revision by revision.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package git-timemachine
  :ensure t
  :commands git-timemachine
  :bind (:map git-timemachine-mode-map
         ("C-j" . git-timemachine-show-next-revision)
         ("C-k" . git-timemachine-show-previous-revision)))
#+end_src

